WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.006 --> 00:00:16.321
Ben stared at the hot sauce overflowing the pot.

2
00:00:16.322 --> 00:00:19.642
"Why is the hot sauce growing?" he cried.

3
00:00:19.643 --> 00:00:24.339
Waldo was fumbling with his glasses.

4
00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:28.899
He jumped back as some hot sauce oozed onto his shoe.

5
00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:31.772
"I—I don't know!" the wizard said.

6
00:00:31.773 --> 00:00:35.501
He put his glasses on and picked up the jar of enhancer.

7
00:00:35.502 --> 00:00:39.464
He peered at the label and then slapped himself on the forehead.

8
00:00:39.465 --> 00:00:44.323
"This isn't enhancer! It's expander."

9
00:00:44.324 --> 00:00:47.821
"What does expander do?" Ben asked.

10
00:00:47.822 --> 00:00:50.562
"What do you think it does?" Waldo said.

11
00:00:50.563 --> 00:00:54.780
"It expands things—it makes them bigger!"

12
00:00:54.781 --> 00:01:05.062
"Ugh." Ben watched helplessly as the sauce flowed across the floor toward a cabinet.

13
00:01:05.063 --> 00:01:07.003
"What are we going to do?"

14
00:01:07.004 --> 00:01:13.155
Waldo sighed. "It'll stop in a few minutes—when the pot is empty."

15
00:01:13.156 --> 00:01:19.165
Waldo was right. Soon the sauce stopped expanding.

16
00:01:19.166 --> 00:01:23.223
Ben grabbed some rags.

17
00:01:23.224 --> 00:01:27.191
"We'd better clean up this mess."

18
00:01:27.192 --> 00:01:37.831
Waldo found a mop, and ten minutes later the floor was clean.

19
00:01:37.848 --> 00:01:45.719
Waldo ladled out some hot sauce from the pot and poured it into a small bottle.

20
00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:47.909
He handed it to Ben.

21
00:01:47.910 --> 00:01:51.909
"Put this in your food tomorrow in Cooking class," the wizard said.

22
00:01:51.910 --> 00:01:56.094
"By the time the bell rings, you'll be out of the cooking competition.

23
00:01:56.095 --> 00:01:59.554
Now we have just one more thing to do."

24
00:01:59.555 --> 00:02:02.281
"We're not done?" Ben asked.

25
00:02:02.282 --> 00:02:04.451
"Nope," Waldo said.

26
00:02:04.452 --> 00:02:10.176
"You need a backup plan, just in case Mr. Icky likes spicy food."

27
00:02:10.177 --> 00:02:15.281
He pulled his large spell book out of his backpack.

28
00:02:15.282 --> 00:02:19.959
"What kind of spell are you looking for?" Ben asked.

29
00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:25.228
"How about a spell that makes your food explode?"

30
00:02:25.229 --> 00:02:30.153
"That won't work," Ben said. "Everyone loves exploding food."

31
00:02:30.154 --> 00:02:33.264
"People don't," Waldo said.

32
00:02:33.265 --> 00:02:38.198
"Mayor Hubbletree was furious when those pizzas exploded, remember?"

33
00:02:38.199 --> 00:02:42.268
Ben shrugged. "But Mr. Icky won't mind that.

34
00:02:42.269 --> 00:02:48.879
I need something that will convince him I'm not good enough to be on Kids' Kitchen Showdown."

35
00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:53.066
"Right." Waldo flipped through more pages.

36
00:02:53.067 --> 00:02:59.687
"Here's a good one. With this spell, any food you touch will disappear."

37
00:02:59.688 --> 00:03:01.894
"That's no good," Ben said.

38
00:03:01.895 --> 00:03:05.593
"I need to cook bad food. Not no food."

39
00:03:05.594 --> 00:03:10.689
"Hmm." Waldo examined another page in his book.

40
00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:15.182
"What if everything you cooked smelled like rotting garbage?"

41
00:03:15.183 --> 00:03:18.823
"What would be so bad about that?" Ben asked.

42
00:03:18.824 --> 00:03:21.158
"I guess nothing," Waldo said.

43
00:03:21.159 --> 00:03:24.307
He turned another page and bent down over his book.

44
00:03:24.308 --> 00:03:29.574
"Oh, this would be perfect. Rotting fish!"

45
00:03:29.575 --> 00:03:34.492
"Eww," Ben said. "That's disgusting."

46
00:03:34.493 --> 00:03:37.284
"It sure is," Waldo agreed.

47
00:03:37.285 --> 00:03:41.384
"Everyone hates the smell of rotting fish—even monsters."

48
00:03:41.385 --> 00:03:45.326
Ben nodded. "Let's do it."

49
00:03:45.327 --> 00:03:50.310
Waldo studied the spell for a moment, quietly murmuring the words.

50
00:03:50.311 --> 00:03:52.591
Finally he stood up.

51
00:03:52.592 --> 00:03:55.557
He pulled out his wand and pointed it at Ben.

52
00:03:55.558 --> 00:04:01.928
As Waldo muttered the magical words, green light flashed from his wand.

53
00:04:01.929 --> 00:04:09.356
Ben felt a strange, tingling sensation. "Did it work?"

54
00:04:09.357 --> 00:04:11.429
"Probably," Waldo said.

55
00:04:11.430 --> 00:04:16.177
"But we won't know until you cook some—" Waldo sniffed.

56
00:04:16.178 --> 00:04:18.772
"Ugh! What's that smell?"

57
00:04:18.773 --> 00:04:24.544
Ben sniffed. "I think it's me."

58
00:04:24.545 --> 00:04:27.707
He smelled his arm.

59
00:04:27.708 --> 00:04:32.450
"Oh no! It is me! I smell like rotting fish!

60
00:04:32.451 --> 00:04:37.872
You messed up the spell—you made me smell like rotting fish!"

61
00:04:37.873 --> 00:04:43.487
"Oops." Waldo looked in his spell book. "I wonder what I did wrong."

62
00:04:43.488 --> 00:04:46.954
Just then Mr. Freaky made an announcement.

63
00:04:46.955 --> 00:04:50.242
"Mr. Bog is going to lock the doors in ten minutes.

64
00:04:50.243 --> 00:04:54.403
All students must leave the building at once."

65
00:04:54.404 --> 00:05:00.911
Ben sighed. "We have to go home, Waldo."

66
00:05:00.912 --> 00:05:07.076
As Ben floated into the corridor, a few monsters immediately cleared out of his way.

67
00:05:07.077 --> 00:05:09.525
"Yuck!" a mummy said.

68
00:05:09.526 --> 00:05:14.851
A ghoul covered her nose. "What smells so bad?"

69
00:05:14.852 --> 00:05:17.643
A fish monster didn't mind the smell though.

70
00:05:17.644 --> 00:05:21.401
"Mmm! It smells like my cousin's house!"

71
00:05:21.402 --> 00:05:25.474
Ben was glad that Winnie wasn't anywhere in sight.

72
00:05:25.475 --> 00:05:29.757
But as he hurried toward an exit, he spotted her.

73
00:05:29.758 --> 00:05:41.391
She must have stayed after school for broom-flying practice.

74
00:05:41.392 --> 00:05:44.181
"Ben!" Winnie ran to catch up to him.

75
00:05:44.182 --> 00:05:47.983
When she reached him, she covered her nose.

76
00:05:47.984 --> 00:05:50.874
"What's that horrible smell?"

77
00:05:50.875 --> 00:05:53.500
"It's me," Ben blurted out.

78
00:05:53.501 --> 00:05:57.759
"Waldo was trying to cast a spell, but he didn't do it right."

79
00:05:57.760 --> 00:06:00.177
"What kind of spell?"

80
00:06:00.178 --> 00:06:07.886
Ben watched the expression on Winnie's face change as he explained about the hot sauce and the rotten fish spell.

81
00:06:07.887 --> 00:06:11.044
Right away he knew she didn't approve.

82
00:06:11.045 --> 00:06:13.375
"I can't believe you'd do that, Ben!

83
00:06:13.376 --> 00:06:17.533
Do you know how many kids would love to be on that show?

84
00:06:17.534 --> 00:06:19.796
Monsters are jealous of you.

85
00:06:19.797 --> 00:06:24.274
And here you are, trying to sabotage yourself.

86
00:06:24.275 --> 00:06:26.550
You should be ashamed!"

87
00:06:26.551 --> 00:06:31.452
Ben sighed, staring down at the ground.

88
00:06:31.453 --> 00:06:36.111
"Mr. Icky picked you for a reason," Winnie went on.

89
00:06:36.112 --> 00:06:39.905
"You have to compete. It's the right thing to do."

90
00:06:39.906 --> 00:06:46.868
Ben sighed. "You're right, Winnie. I'll do the show."

91
00:06:46.869 --> 00:06:49.566
Winnie smiled. "Good!"

92
00:06:49.567 --> 00:07:02.602
Ben sniffed. "But right now I need to get home and take a shower!"
